+## Runtime invariants
 
-The pinned official Qwen3.5 graph already supports `cls.output.weight`. We store its 255 BF16 rows directly, in the canonical GLiDE readout order. `qwen35.embedding_length_out=255`, `qwen35.pooling_type=LAST`, and a context configured with embeddings enabled make the graph expose the last-position raw projection via `llama_get_embeddings_seq(ctx, 0)`.
+The context explicitly requests `LLAMA_FLASH_ATTN_TYPE_ENABLED`, never AUTO; F16 K/V; one noncausal whole-prompt decode; `n_batch=n_ubatch=configured context`; all positional output rows; LAST pooling; and raw finite 255 logits. Prefix reuse and prompt truncation are prohibited. KV and recurrent memory are cleared before and after every attempted evaluation, including exception/abort cleanup. The reset flags become true only after the clear calls return.
 
-The word “embeddings” is only the upstream API transport here. **The 255 returned values are unnormalized raw logits.** There is no softmax, sampler, generation, or normalization in this runner. The LAST pooling path gathers the final positional row. The normal vocabulary LM head is not expanded into the computation graph in this mode. The unused model-loader token-embedding fallback does not allocate an expanded vocabulary-sized GLiDE head.
